{
  "name": "Riley Content System - Approval & Scheduling",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "content-approval",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "webhook-approval",
      "name": "Webhook: Approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [0, 200],
      "webhookId": "content-approval"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Approval Workflow\n\nThis workflow handles content approval, scheduling, AND learning.\n\n**Trigger:** Webhook POST to /content-approval\n\n**Payload:**\n```json\n{\n  \"week_date\": \"2024-01-15\",\n  \"status\": \"approved\" | \"needs_edits\",\n  \"topic\": \"Field Guide Topic\",\n  \"field_guide\": \"Full field guide text\",\n  \"edits\": [optional array of edit requests]\n}\n```\n\n**Actions:**\n- If approved: Schedule to Hypefury → Trigger Self-Learning\n- If needs edits: Send back for revision\n\n**Self-Learning:** Approved content is stored in Supabase with embeddings for future retrieval.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "sticky-approval",
      "name": "Workflow Info",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-200, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "approved-check",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.status }}",
              "rightValue": "approved",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "check-status",
      "name": "Check Approval Status",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [200, 200]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "filePath": "={{ '/files/outputs/weekly/' + $json.body.week_date + '/calendar.md' }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "read-calendar",
      "name": "Read Calendar",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.readWriteFile",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [400, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "chat",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are a content scheduling assistant. Parse the content calendar and extract tweets and posts for scheduling.\n\nOutput format for each item:\n{\n  \"platform\": \"twitter\" | \"linkedin\",\n  \"content\": \"full text\",\n  \"scheduled_time\": \"ISO datetime\",\n  \"type\": \"tweet\" | \"thread\" | \"linkedin_post\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "=CALENDAR:\n{{ $json.data }}\n\nExtract all content items with their scheduled times.\nOutput as JSON array sorted by scheduled_time."
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "maxTokens": 8192,
          "temperature": 0.1
        }
      },
      "id": "parse-schedule",
      "name": "Parse Schedule",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [600, 100],
      "credentials": {
        "anthropicApi": {
          "id": "anthropic-creds",
          "name": "Anthropic API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse the scheduled content into individual items\nconst content = JSON.parse($input.first().json.message.content);\n\n// Return each item as a separate output\nreturn content.map(item => ({\n  json: item\n}));"
      },
      "id": "split-items",
      "name": "Split Into Items",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [800, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "platform-check",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.platform }}",
              "rightValue": "twitter",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "route-platform",
      "name": "Route by Platform",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1000, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.hypefury.com/api/v1/posts",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "text",
              "value": "={{ $json.content }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "scheduled_time",
              "value": "={{ $json.scheduled_time }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "schedule-hypefury",
      "name": "Schedule to Hypefury",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.1,
      "position": [1200, 0],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "hypefury-creds",
          "name": "Hypefury API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## LinkedIn Scheduling Note\n\nLinkedIn API requires OAuth and has posting limits.\n\nOptions:\n1. Use LinkedIn API directly (complex setup)\n2. Use Buffer or Hootsuite API\n3. Manual scheduling with notification\n\nCurrent: Manual notification with content to copy.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 350
      },
      "id": "linkedin-note",
      "name": "LinkedIn Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1100, 250]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "linkedin-queue",
              "name": "linkedin_posts",
              "value": "={{ $json }}",
              "type": "object"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "queue-linkedin",
      "name": "Queue LinkedIn Posts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.3,
      "position": [1200, 200]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "combine",
        "combineBy": "combineAll",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "merge-results",
      "name": "Merge Results",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [1400, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.slack_webhook || 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/YOUR/WEBHOOK/URL' }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "text",
              "value": "=✅ Content scheduled successfully!\n\n📅 Week of: {{ $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.week_date }}\n📱 Twitter posts: Scheduled in Hypefury\n💼 LinkedIn posts: Ready in queue (manual post required)\n\n🔗 Check Hypefury dashboard to confirm."
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "notify-success",
      "name": "Notify: Scheduled",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.1,
      "position": [1600, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.WEBHOOK_URL || 'http://localhost:5678' }}/webhook/learn-content",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ {\n  \"week_date\": $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.week_date,\n  \"topic\": $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.topic || 'Unknown Topic',\n  \"content_items\": JSON.parse($('Split Into Items').first().json.message?.content || '[]'),\n  \"field_guide\": $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.field_guide || ''\n} }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      },
      "id": "trigger-learning",
      "name": "Trigger Learning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.1,
      "position": [1700, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ {\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"message\": \"Content scheduled and learned successfully\",\n  \"week_date\": $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.week_date,\n  \"items_scheduled\": $json.length,\n  \"learning_triggered\": true\n} }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "respond-success",
      "name": "Respond: Success",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1900, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Webhook: Approval').item.json.body.slack_webhook || 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/YOUR/WEBHOOK/URL' }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "text",
              "value": "=📝 Content needs edits\n\n📅 Week of: {{ $json.body.week_date }}\n\nRequested edits:\n{{ $json.body.edits ? $json.body.edits.join('\\n• ') : 'No specific edits provided' }}\n\nPlease update the content and re-submit for approval."
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "notify-edits",
      "name": "Notify: Needs Edits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.1,
      "position": [400, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ {\n  \"status\": \"needs_edits\",\n  \"message\": \"Content sent back for revision\",\n  \"week_date\": $json.body.week_date,\n  \"edits\": $json.body.edits || []\n} }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "respond-edits",
      "name": "Respond: Needs Edits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [600, 300]
    }
  ],
